    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=48&rid=40075": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Mo",
      "description": "Department: Music - HSU\nAssistant Professor 9 Mo | Working Title | Assistant Professor of Music in Applied Woodwinds | Position # | F00052 | Department | Music - HSU\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Music in Applied Woodwinds Position # F00052 Department Music - HSU Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Henderson State University Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with education and experience Closing: 12/9/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Assistant Professor of Music in Applied Woodwinds. Nine-month appointment. The appointment will be tenure track if the appointee has an earned doctorate. Duties & Responsibilities: Applied instruction, woodwind methods, woodwind ensemble, and advising woodwind majors. Instruction of other academic courses (i.e. music theory and/or history) according to the creative expertise of the candidate/ innovative needs of the program. Additional responsibilities may include but are not limited to ensemble direction and/or assistance, participation in program and university committees, recruiting. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Experience in jazz is a plus. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Other: THE DEPARTMENT: The Program of Music at Henderson State University consists of nine full-time and seven part-time faculty members. The program offers the Bachelor of Music degree with tracks in Performance and Music Education, and a Bachelor of Arts in Music to approximately 70 music majors from Arkansas and Texas. It is housed in the Russell Fine Arts Building, which includes the 214-seat Harwood Recital Hall, the Evanson Band Hall, and piano and computer labs. It is a fully accredited member of the National Association of Schools of Music (NASM). For more information, visit www.hsu.edu/music. THE UNIVERSITY: Henderson is located in Arkadelphia, AR, a charming community of 11,000 residents situated less than an hour south of Little Rock. Nestled in the foothills of the Ouachita Mountains, the community is home to two universities, a strong public school system, a thriving medical community, two recreational rivers, the iconic DeGray Lake, and is approximately 30 miles from historic Hot Springs National Park, one of the great American treasures. Please visit www.hsu.edu, www.arkadelphiaalliance.com, or www.arkadelphiaschools.org for more information about Henderson and our community. APPLICATION: The review of applications will begin December 15, 2026. Application materials must be submitted electronically to Dr. Heather Thayer, Chair, Woodwinds Search at thayerh@hsu.edu. To be considered, each applicant must provide: 1) a letter of application 2) curriculum vitae 3) unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts 4) a document with links to three to five digital recordings that display the candidate’s musicianship: a) solo performance (required) b) chamber or large ensemble performance (required) c) conducting (optional) 5) a document with complete contact information for three references who can speak to the candidate’s teaching abilities. The final applicant for this position will be required to submit to a background screening, including a criminal background check, pursuant to university policy. The applicant will also be required to provide official transcripts to Human Resources. Under the provisions of the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act, applications are subject to public inspection upon written request. Minimum Qualifications: Henderson State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer/ Affirmative Action Employer with a significant commitment to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its faculty, staff and students. Successful candidates will have (at minimum) a terminal master’s degree and/or a Ph.D. from an accredited institution of higher education, and at least one year of teaching experience at the collegiate level. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Share Apply Now"
    },
